Patches SuiteSparse 7.3.1 for the powsybl-math-native build.

Three things are done here, all for the same underlying reason - SuiteSparse is
built as a nested FetchContent sub-project rather than standalone:

1. CHOLMOD/CMakeLists.txt: comment out the NCHECK / NMATRIXOPS / NCHOLESKY /
   NMODIFY "module existence" guards.

   Each guard reads `if ( NOT EXISTS ${CMAKE_SOURCE_DIR}/<Module> )` and
   disables the module when the directory is absent. CMAKE_SOURCE_DIR is the
   *top-level* source dir, which here is the powsybl-math-native root, not
   CHOLMOD's own directory - so those paths never exist and every guard
   misfires, silently compiling out modules we need (Cholesky above all).
   Commenting them out lets the NCHECK/... options keep their real defaults.
   Upstream would use CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR; we do not touch the guard for
   Supernodal, which we *do* want disabled - see 2.

2. A top-level CMakeLists.txt is added (it does not exist in the tarball, which
   expects each module to be built separately). It pulls in only the modules we
   need, and force-disables CHOLMOD's Supernodal module: Supernodal is the only
   component requiring BLAS/LAPACK, and the Gauss-Newton solver uses the
   BLAS-free simplicial factorization instead. This keeps the build portable,
   notably on Windows where BLAS is painful to provide.

3. SuiteSparse_config/CMakeLists.txt: skip the BLAS/LAPACK detection entirely,
   for the same reason as 2 - none of the modules we build (amd, colamd, btf,
   klu, cxsparse, and CHOLMOD minus Supernodal) link against it.

